                "name": "Buck",
                "type": "action",
                "img": "icons/svg/mystery-man.svg",
                "data": {
                  "description": {
                    "value": "[reaction] DC 17<br>Most monsters that serve as mounts can attempt to\nbuck off unwanted or annoying riders, but most mounts\nwill not use this reaction against a trusted creature unless\nthe mounts are spooked or mistreated. <b>Trigger</b> A creature\nMounts or uses the Command an Animal action while riding\nthe monster. <b>Effect</b> The triggering creature must succeed\nat a Reflex saving throw against the listed DC or fall off the\ncreature and land prone. If the save is a critical failure, the\ntriggering creature also takes [[/r 1d6 # bludgeoning damage]] bludgeoning damage in\naddition to the normal damage for the fall.",
                    "chat": "",
                    "unidentified": ""
                  },
